// Certified Residential Specialist — a designation awarded by the Residential Real Estate Council that sits ON TOP OF an active state real estate license.
//
// Read src/data/tracks/CONTRACT.md before editing. The sourcing rule is the product.
// Two things this file has to keep straight, because generic prep material blurs both:
//
//   1. The CRS is NOT a license. Nobody can earn it without already holding an active
//      state real estate license and active RRC membership. globalSpec below describes the
//      credential itself; stateSpecs describes the license underneath it.
//   2. There is NO proctored CRS exam. The designation is awarded on completed RRC
//      coursework plus a documented production or experience record. Anyone who tells a
//      candidate to 'study for the CRS exam' is selling something that does not exist.
//
// The stateSpecs block is the UNDERLYING STATE SALESPERSON/BROKER LICENSE and is shared
// byte-for-byte with crs.js, rene.js, psa.js and epro.js — the license is the same
// whichever credential sits on top. 'unconfirmed' means no primary source published it;
// verified:true means the entry is an honest secondary-source compilation.

